## Documents to be obtained :-
i. Claim form (Annex I-B) duly filled in and signed by the claimant(s) other than those who have signed the letter of disclaimer/ no objection;
ii. Death certificate of the deceased depositor(s);
iii. Officially Valid Document of the claimant(s) towards verifying his/ her identity and address;
iv. Bond of indemnity (Annex I-C) signed by the claimant(s);
v. Letter of disclaimer/ no objection (Annex I-D) from non-claimant legal heir(s), and
vi. Legal Heir Certificate issued by a competent authority OR Declaration (Annex I-E) regarding the legal heir(s) of the deceased depositor(s) by an independent person who is well known to the family of the deceased, is not a party to the claim and is acceptable to the bank.
vii. No bond of surety from a third party in case of claims up to the threshold limit.

